          "path": "_m/t/c/b/m/saraswathi-mahal-library-wp/1468-ce-paper-manuscript-sansk.jpg",
          "filename": "1468 CE paper manuscript, Sanskrit, bhasya on Adi Shankara's Advaita bhasya, Varanasi, India.jpg",
          "caption": "A palm leaf manuscript page in Sanskrit language, produced in 1468 CE. It is a commentary on \"a commentary by the early 9th-century Hindu philosopher Adi Shankara\". \nThis manuscript is preserved at the Saraswathi Mahal Library, Thanjavur, Tamil Nadu, India. \nThe Saraswathi Mahal Library has nearly 50,000 historic manuscripts, a portion of which are rare, mostly in Sanskrit and Tamil. A large portion of its collection has not been published.\nIt is digitizing its manuscripts collection, and participating in the many historic manuscripts digitization initiatives underway in India and Nepal in public, private and monastic institutions.\n\nThis is a photograph of a 2-D manuscript page produced in the 15th-century. Wikimedia commons PD-Art licensing guidelines apply.",
          "alt": "A palm leaf manuscript page in Sanskrit language, produced in 1468 CE. It is a commentary on \"a commentary by the early 9th-century Hindu philosopher Adi Shankara\". \nThis manuscript is preserved at the Saraswathi Mahal Library, Thanjavur, Tamil Nadu, India. \nThe Saraswathi Mahal Library has nearly 50,000 historic manuscripts, a portion of which are rare, mostly in Sanskrit and Tamil. A large portion of its collection has not been published.\nIt is digitizing its manuscripts collection, and participating in the many historic manuscripts digitization initiatives underway in India and Nepal in public, private and monastic institutions.\n\nThis is a photograph of a 2-D manuscript page produced in the 15th-century. Wikimedia commons PD-Art licensing guidelines apply.",
          "width": 1464,
