          "path": "_m/t/c/b/m/saraswathi-mahal-library-wp/mural-paintings-at-sarawati-ma.jpg",
          "filename": "Mural Paintings at Sarawati Mahal Libray Thanjavur India.jpg",
          "caption": "The exquisite art work adorns the ceilings of Saraswathi Mahal Library. The Library is a treasure trove for literary and artistic lovers and it consists of a rare collection of Palm leaf manuscripts and paper written in Tamil, Hindi, Telugu, Marathi, English and a few other languages indigenous to India. It was started as a Royal Library for the private pleasure of the Nayak Kings of Thanjavur who ruled 1535 - 1675 AD.",
